Found while measuring karr #56 (sops 3.13.3, Perl 5.36.0, Cpanel::JSON::XS 4.40, JSON::XS 4.04, JSON::PP 4.16, YAML::XS 0.904.0).

File::SOPS::Encrypted::value_to_bytes writes a float as strconv.FormatFloat(v, "f", -1, 64) -- the SHORTEST decimal that round-trips, up to 17 significant digits. That is what the MAC digest covers. Every emitter this distribution has writes the same double with 15 significant digits:

  * Cpanel::JSON::XS, JSON::XS and JSON::PP all render through %.15g (NV_DIG).
  * YAML::XS renders through Perl stringification, which is also 15.

For any double that needs 16 or 17 digits the document therefore says one number and the digest covers another. Measured end to end, default configuration, unencrypted_suffix (no config needed):

  value 0.1+0.2   digest 0.30000000000000004   emitted 0.3                 self MAC FAIL, sops -d exit 51
  value 1/3       digest 0.3333333333333333    emitted 0.333333333333333   self MAC FAIL, sops -d exit 51

Both formats, all three JSON backends, so this is not the backend question of #56 -- it survives ADR 0005.

sops itself writes such a value at full precision ("sum_unencrypted": 0.30000000000000004) and reads it back, exit 0, so the reference has no such defect and a sops-written document with one of these values is readable here.

Only UNENCRYPTED floats are affected: an encrypted value is an ENC[...] string on the wire, and its plaintext is the digest bytes by construction.

Not attempted under #56 because a fix moves wire bytes for both formats and needs its own ADR. Options, none measured yet:
  a) emit floats ourselves as the same canonical form value_to_bytes uses (JSON has no portable raw-number injection -- all three backends quote a scalar that carries a PV -- so this likely means a wrapper class per format handler, or a post-pass over the emitted text)
  b) hash what the emitter will actually write, i.e. derive the digest from the document rather than from the tree (inverts ADR 0001s direction and breaks the encrypt sides sorted-key walk)
  c) refuse to write a float that does not survive its own emitter, at assert_representable, and say so -- fails loud, loses no data, writes no bad document
Wire lane.
